  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Find the average value ${f}_{\\text{avg}}$ of the function $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(3x)$ on the interval $[0,\\frac{\\pi }{3}].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}_{\\text{avg}}=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(\\frac{\\pi }{3}-0)}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{3}{\\pi }(-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(3x)}{3})|}_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\pi }[(-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\pi ))-(-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(0))] \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\pi }[(-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot (-1))-(-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 1)] \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\pi }(\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{2}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
